# stepper_ipropi_worst.test's detent compensation check on its own: at
# 0.2 rev/s with the DRV8876's worst-case IPROPI errors, switching
# stp_ttc0.detent on mid-move stick-slips in most phases (following error
# ~0.055 rad at ~0.2 A, then a jerk: ~10000 rad/s^2 of acceleration span
# against ~1360 when it doesn't). Which one depends on the phase: shifting
# the start by one rt cycle flips it, on the code before this branch too
# (DEBUGNOTES "brdstepper: detent compensation stick-slips").
@todo detent compensation stick-slips with worst-case IPROPI (DEBUGNOTES)
@args --drive tests/nema11/stmbl.conf --sim tests/nema11/sim_ipropi_worst.txt
@timeout 180
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
fault0.state
@sample pid0.pos_error 0.001 0.2
lcnc 1 10
run 1
@sample pid0.pos_error 0.001 0.3
@sample hv0.abs_volt 0.001 0.3
hv0.sim_vel
lcnc 1 0
run 1
hv0.sim_load = 0.047
run 0.5
hv0.iq_fb
pid0.pos_error
pe0.p_el_ac
hv0.sim_load = 0
run 0.5
stp_ttc0.detent = 0
lcnc 1 0.2
run 1
@sample stp_ttc0.cur 0.0005 0.5
@sample hv0.sim_acc 0.0005 0.5
stp_ttc0.detent = 0.004
run 0.5
@sample hv0.sim_acc 0.0005 0.5
@expect span hv0.sim_acc[1:1000] > 2000
@expect span hv0.sim_acc[1001:2000] < 2000
